# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/packages/
# (quick task 260828-75k). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (see modules/security/qmldir, modules/osd/qmldir,
# modules/lock/qmldir): any .qml type added to this directory that is NOT
# declared below becomes unresolvable, with no load error — it simply
# reads `undefined` forever. qml-import-check enforces this. Any FUTURE
# type added here MUST be declared in the same commit that creates it.
#
# ── THE `singleton` KEYWORD IS LOAD-BEARING ───────────────────────────
# PackagesBackend carries `pragma Singleton` AND is marked `singleton`
# below. modules/qmldir's own header records why both are required,
# binary-verified in 12-06: without the qmldir keyword, a bare
# `PackagesBackend.packages`-style access resolves to `undefined`
# forever and the object is never constructed. Removing either one is a
# silent, error-free failure.
#
# PackagesBackend is the singleton that owns the whole package model.
# The workbench window, the Settings page, the launcher's `pkg` route
# and the bar capsule are FOUR READERS OF ONE BACKEND, never four
# backends — and it is a singleton specifically so a long-running read
# or a pending preview outlives the surface that asked for it.
module qs.modules.packages

singleton PackagesBackend 1.0 PackagesBackend.qml

# ── Surfaces ──
# D4, the main surface: its own FloatingWindow behind a LazyLoader, the
# FilePicker pattern. NOT a singleton — shell.qml mounts one instance, the
# same posture Bar/Dashboard/Overview have in modules/qmldir.
Workbench 1.0 Workbench.qml

# The workbench's three panes, split the way FilePicker splits its own
# (FpSidebar / FpFolderContents / FpFooter) rather than one 1000-line file.
WbSidebar 1.0 WbSidebar.qml
WbTable 1.0 WbTable.qml
WbDetail 1.0 WbDetail.qml

# One button shape for all three panes, so a disabled action explains
# itself the same way everywhere.
WbButton 1.0 WbButton.qml
